   "note": "the figure of chapter 57, the «brick» for observing, drawn by hand in the print: a square frame with the letters ا, ب, ج, د outside its corners (upper right, upper left, lower right, lower left); about the corner ا a quarter circle from the upper side to the right side, made of a heavy arc, a thin arc close outside it, the band of eighteen cells with the numbers 5 to 90 in letters (ه, ي, يه, ك, كه, ل, له, م, مه, ن, نه, س, سه, ع, عه, ف, فه, ص, from the upper side downward, their heads toward the outside), and the ladder of the single parts, eighty-nine steps between two arcs; a straight line from the corner ا to the heavy arc at 45 parts; outside the ladder, at the middle of the quarter, the small oblong of the piece ط with a line across its middle and the letter ل in its lower half, and ط beside it; ه left of the frame near its upper left corner and ز inside its lower left corner (the ends of the line of midday), ح left of the scale at about 26 parts and ك under it at about 65 parts. Measured on the master scan at 1200 dpi: the corners of the frame, the four arcs (each with its own centre, a hand's breadth of 0.6 pt apart), the borders of the cells and the steps of the ladder from the ink along the middle of each band, the sides of the oblong. The steps at 31, 38, 42, 54 and 65 parts are printed faint or in part and are drawn whole. The labels are set in the type of the edition at the centres of their printed ink, turned as printed; the hand of the numbers is not imitated"
